# Dev tooling with no runtime purpose. These configure the linters and test
# runners used to BUILD the extension; a user's install has no linter and no
# test runner to configure, so they were shipping 5 KB of noise to every seat.
.markdownlint.json
.pre-commit-config.yaml
optimize-gif.js
eslint.config.mjs
package-lock.json
node_modules/**
.pytest_cache/**
*.vsix
**/*.ts
**/*.map
.architect/**
# Gitignored locally, so a CI build (which packages a clean git checkout)
# never sees them — but a local `vsce package` does, and would ship internal
# governance material and a coverage report to every Marketplace user.
.claude/**
.gemini/**
.human/**
.zenzic-score.json
.zenzic-history.jsonl
.DS_Store
coverage/**
.zenzic_cache/**
example/**
_zenzic_core/**
# A local Python virtualenv at the repository root. CI never has one here (it
# syncs the core into _zenzic_core/, excluded above), so CI's VSIX is clean and
# its 5 MB size guard never fired -- but `vsce package` run on a developer
# machine that has one would ship every file in it. Found by listing what the
# packaged VSIX actually contains rather than trusting the guard that had never
# been given the chance to fail.
.venv/**
# Compiled extension-host test code. `tests/**` and `tsconfig.host-test.json`
# are already excluded above; this is the same material after `tsc`, and it
# additionally carries a runtime `require('glob')` that resolves only through a
# devDependency. The suite runs from the working tree, never from the VSIX.
out/test/**
# The demo-capture sandbox is build/marketing tooling, not extension runtime:
# it is committed (unlike .claude/), but a Marketplace user has no use for it
# and it would ship a Dockerfile inside every install (Rule 30 -- .gitignore
# and the packaging manifest are different files and neither implies the other).
docker/**
ROADMAP.md
images/demo*.gif
